    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Social/Emotional:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " smiles on his own to get your attention; chuckles (not yet a full laugh) when you try to make him laugh; looks at you, moves, or makes sounds to get or keep your attention. "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Language/Communication:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " makes sounds like \"oooo,\" \"aahh\" (cooing); makes sounds back when you talk to him; turns head toward the sound of your voice. "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cognitive:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " if hungry, opens mouth when he sees breast or bottle; looks at her hands with interest. "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Movement/Physical:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " holds head steady without support when you are holding him; holds a toy when you put it in his hand; uses his arm to swing at toys; brings hands to mouth; pushes up onto elbows/forearms when on tummy. [S3]"
     }
    ]
   },
